From: lutvzn <106083845+lutvzn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:31:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] qualcommax: ipq50xx: redmi-ax3000: keep the CPU at 1008
 MHz

Since 0974 the CPU boosts to 1296 MHz under load at the same fixed 1.1 V
(no CPU regulator). On the RA81's IPQ5000 that corrupts memory under
network load: single bits cleared (mostly bit 42 of a 64-bit word, at
offset 8 of a cache line), oopses on kernel pointers with bit 42
cleared, and silent resets every few minutes under Wi-Fi downlink.
Pinned at 1296 MHz the board reset 1.5 s into a 400 Mbit/s downlink;
capped at 1008 MHz, the same load ran 20 min with no error in a 24 MB
RAM test (7 errors in 15 min with the boost).

1008 MHz is also the highest operating point of the vendor firmware
(800 and 1008 MHz at 1.1 V), and with TSENS off nothing would throttle.
Drop the 1296 MHz operating point on this board.
---
 .../linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts   | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts b/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts
index 20f211425a..5fdcde3792 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-redmi-ax3000.dts
@@ -110,6 +110,19 @@
 	reg = <0x0 0x40000000 0x0 0x800000>;
 };
 
+/*
+ * Keep the CPU at the rated 1008 MHz, the highest operating point of the
+ * vendor firmware (800 and 1008 MHz at 1.1 V). There is no CPU regulator,
+ * and with TSENS off (below) no thermal throttling either. Boosting to
+ * 1296 MHz at the same 1.1 V corrupted memory on this IPQ5000 under
+ * network load: single bits cleared (mostly bit 42 of a 64-bit word),
+ * kernel oopses on pointers and silent resets every few minutes, none
+ * at 1008 MHz.
+ */
+&cpu_opp_table {
+	/delete-node/ opp-1296000000;
+};
+
 &sleep_clk {
 	clock-frequency = <32000>;
 };
